# Build your own Claude Code (course repo)

This workspace is **Codecrafters course content** (`codecrafters-io/build-your-own-claude-code`), not a single learner checkout.

## Canonical specs

- Stages and slugs: `course-definition.yml`
- Learner-facing instructions: `stage_descriptions/`
- Skills extension design: `extension_designs/skills.md`

## Tools the learner implements (final state)

`Read`, `Write`, `Bash`, and `Skill`, with an OpenAI-compatible agent loop and OpenRouter.

## Skills behavior (match stages, then Claude Code)

- Discover `.claude/skills/*/SKILL.md`; catalog = name + description only in system prompt
- User `/name` and stacked `/a /b args` with `$ARGUMENTS` / `$N` substitution
- Script skills: prefix invocation with skill folder location when body references `scripts/`
- Model invokes via `Skill` tool; `context: fork` runs body in a nested agent loop

## Local full-feature reference

`playground/rust/` (preferred on Mac Studio Ultra) and `playground/python/` implement all base tools + skills extension. Run from repo:

```bash
cd playground/rust && ./your_program.sh -p "..."
# playground/.env → OLLAMA_BASE_URL=https://ollama.tokenizin.com/v1
```

Project skills for real Claude Code / testing: `.claude/skills/`.

When editing course content, keep **one source of truth** for behavior in stage descriptions; update both playgrounds when stages change.
